1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
y = mx + b. What is it FOR? You wondered at 14. Nobody answered.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:06,400
A small shop. Four days of sales: 30, 40, 50, 60. Four dots. That is all the data.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,200
Look at the step from one day to the next. Ten more. Ten more. Ten more. It never changes. That step is m. m = 10.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:16,000
Join the dots and you get one straight line. Run it backwards, past day one, to where it started: 20. That is b. b = 20.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,200
So the line is y = 10x + 20. The step is 10, the start is 20. That is the entire line.

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,200
Now run it one more day. Day 5: ten times five, plus twenty. Seventy. Tomorrow you sell 70. You just predicted the future.

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,000
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,800
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
